From 9b6f7146908332d56341e1a379e977e215e6212a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusheng Zheng <yunwei356@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:06:47 +0000
Subject: [RFC PATCH bpf-next v1 1/5] bpf: Add verified kinsn descriptors and
 proof lowering

Ordinary kfunc calls impose a call boundary even when an operation can be
emitted as a few native instructions. Provide a registered descriptor that
supplies a BPF proof sequence for verification and a bounded native emitter
for JIT execution.

Bind descriptors to explicit kfunc BTF IDs, apply the usual kfunc allow
policy, and reject flags whose call semantics cannot survive lowering.
Decode a preceding sidecar as a 52-bit payload, lower each call to its
proof, verify the resulting program, and restore the original pair for JIT
compilation. Record callee-saved registers used by proofs.

Require a GPL-compatible program and an architecture that advertises kinsn
JIT support. Default that capability to false so a proof cannot be accepted
before its native JIT support is available. Print sidecar payloads in
disassembly and keep the tools UAPI copy synchronized.
